    {
      "text": "grace and truth came by Jesus, John 1:17. he that doeth truth cometh to the light, John 3:21. worship him in spirit and in truth, John 4:24. know the truth, and the truth shall make you free, John 8:32. devil … abode not in the truth … no truth in him, John 8:44. if I say the truth, why do ye not believe me, John 8:46. I am the way, the truth, and the life, John 14:6. Spirit of truth; whom the world cannot receive, John 14:17. Spirit of truth … shall testify of me, John 15:26. he will guide you into all truth, John 16:13. Sanctify them through thy truth: thy word is truth, John 17:17. I should bear witness unto the truth, John 18:37. Pilate saith … What is truth, John 18:38. changed the truth of God into a lie, Rom. 1:25. them that are contentious, and do not obey the truth, Rom. 2:8. keep the feast … with the unleavened bread of … truth, 1 Cor. 5:8. rejoiceth in the truth, 1 Cor. 13:6. Am I … your enemy, because I tell you the truth, Gal. 4:16. who did hinder you that ye should not obey the truth, Gal. 5:7. trusted, after that ye heard the word of truth, Eph. 1:13. having your loins girt about with truth, Eph. 6:14 (D&C 27:16). church … the pillar and ground of the truth, 1 Tim. 3:15. men … destitute of the truth, 1 Tim. 6:5. never able to come to the knowledge of the truth, 2 Tim. 3:7. withstood Moses, so do these also resist the truth, 2 Tim. 3:8. they shall turn away their ears from the truth, 2 Tim. 4:4. Of his own will begat he us with the word of truth, James 1:18. if any of you do err from the truth, James 5:19. way of truth shall be evil spoken of, 2 Pet. 2:2. If we say that we have no sin … the truth is not in us, 1 Jn. 1:8. no lie is of the truth, 1 Jn. 2:21. Hereby know we the spirit of truth, 1 Jn. 4:6. because the Spirit is truth, 1 Jn. 5:6.",
